  "id": "bmld",
  "term": "BMLD",
  "definition": "BMLD stands for binaural masking-level difference, a laboratory measure of how much using both ears improves detecting a sound in noise. It is the difference in the just-audible level of a signal between two binaural listening conditions, commonly comparing the same-phase condition with one where the signal is phase-inverted at one ear.",
